      {
        "label": "D-1 Cut over the pilot with Postgres logical replication",
        "raw": "/projects/2415ccf7-9c11-4023-b933-f5ab9db037d3/decisions?decision=ed772b25-a0de-45e6-b207-108169f39486",
        "href": "/projects/2415ccf7-9c11-4023-b933-f5ab9db037d3/decisions?decision=ed772b25-a0de-45e6-b207-108169f39486",
        "targetId": "ed772b25-a0de-45e6-b207-108169f39486",
        "resolves": true
      }
    ],
    "answer": "We chose Postgres logical replication for the pilot cut-over because application-layer dual-write would have required touching nineteen write paths in the payments service, which would have taken four to five weeks of work. The rollback benefit of application-layer dual-write was also not needed at pilot volume, where rollback within two to four hours is acceptable. [D-1 Cut over the pilot with Postgres logical replication](/projects/2415ccf7-9c11-4023-b933-f5ab9db037d3/decisions?decision=ed772b25-a0de-45e6-b207-108169f39486)",
    "finishReason": "stop"
  },
